=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_7e3a — Standard dual-WFH; laptop stowed during work; remote on the floor (fork of p_a1b2)

Two remote workers share this home. Both sit at their desks from 9 to 17:30 on weekdays and never leave during work hours. Keys, wallets, and jackets stay at the entry all day. Meals happen at the kitchen table for breakfast and lunch, at the dining table for dinner. In the evening both settle onto the couch for TV from 20:00 to 22:30. On weekends they sleep in until about 10:30, do errands together around midday, and are home the rest of the day. Nothing in this household travels.

What changed from the parent (p_a1b2): (1) Marco's laptop is at desk_b1 but closed or stowed during the 9-to-17 work window — the robot found it only once in twelve looks at the desk during those hours, so I lower the chance to "sometimes" for that window and add a separate "usually" block for the morning (6–9 h) when it is open and visible. (2) The remote is on the living-room floor (floor_l_l1) during and after evening TV, not on the coffee table. The sightings show it on the TV stand at 18:00 (before TV) and on the floor at 22:00 and 03:00 (during/after TV and overnight). I move the 20–22.5 h block to floor_l_l1.

What would refute this fork: Marco's laptop sighted at a location other than desk_b1 at 07:00 on a weekday, or the remote sighted on the TV stand at 21:30 on a weekday.

